From: PowOS <mats@powback.com>
Subject: [PATCH] backends/anland: a window task draws each frame once, an asked full screen waits for its size, X11 windows are offered by their class

Three user reports, 2026-11-02, read off hyprland.log and the app's window-log (no game started for it):

1. Broforce "black noise pattern ... flickering in and out" and low fps: "window task 11 frames: last 5 s 110 commits,
   300 drawn". One commit marked every buffer stale and each offered buffer was drawn again - the same frame composited
   full screen (2268x2440) ~2.7 times, on the GPU the game renders with, and the later draws sampled Xwayland's window
   buffer while the next Present copy wrote it (KGSL: no implicit sync). Now a buffer is drawn only while the window's
   newest content hasn't gone to the consumer yet; the keepalive still draws a stale buffer before it answers, so an
   older frame is never shown. A rescale (refit, fitFullScreen) marks every buffer stale itself.

2. "Trying to fullscreen Broforce, but it doesn't work" (21:35, five taps): on the app's full-screen request the task
   was still the floating one, so 0047 configured the window to 504x606 logical for a moment; the borderless game
   window (covering Wine's monitor) took that as leaving full screen and KWin answered "fullscreen 0". An asked full
   screen now keeps the window's size until the app's full-screen size arrives.

3. "I opened steam and it shows two windows": Steam's X window names no desktop file, so it was offered as "" and the
   app's launch placeholder for "steam" never got it. A window with no desktop file is offered by its WM_CLASS class
   (Steam: "steam"; a Proton game: steam_app_<id>, which the app maps to the entry that starts it).
---
diff --git a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
index bed0c92..8262afc 100644
--- a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
@@ -484,7 +484,7 @@ void AnlandWindowTask::watchWindow(Window *window)
     Watched watched;
     watched.window = window;
     watched.damaged = connect(window, &Window::damaged, this, [this]() {
-        std::fill(std::begin(m_stale), std::end(m_stale), true);
+        markStale();
         m_statCommits++;
         if (!m_damagePending) {
             m_damagePending = true;
@@ -505,11 +505,11 @@ void AnlandWindowTask::watchWindow(Window *window)
                 break;
             }
         }
-        std::fill(std::begin(m_stale), std::end(m_stale), true);
+        markStale();
         scheduleRender();
     });
     m_watched.append(watched);
-    std::fill(std::begin(m_stale), std::end(m_stale), true);
+    markStale();
     scheduleRender();
 }
 
@@ -613,6 +613,7 @@ bool AnlandWindowTask::importBuffers()
         m_fbos[i] = std::move(imported.fbo);
         m_stale[i] = true;
     }
+    m_newestQueued = false;
     m_bufCount = count;
     // KWin's screen is the one the windows are on: placed against a smaller one (the cover screen KWin started on),
     // a client's menus and X11 override-redirect popups landed far from their parent's buttons.
@@ -798,6 +799,7 @@ void AnlandWindowTask::refit()
     qCInfo(KWIN_ANLAND) << "window task" << m_id << "the window took" << has << "itself, the task is" << wanted << ": sized back";
     fitWindow();
     if (fitsWindow()) {
+        markStale(); // PowOS: every buffer, at the new scale (no longer redrawn by a later offer by itself)
         scheduleRender(); // full screen keeps its size: drawn again at the task's new scale
     }
 }
@@ -917,6 +919,7 @@ void AnlandWindowTask::fitFullScreen()
     m_resizeAsked = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
     m_resizeWanted = client;
     m_window->moveResize(RectF(m_window->frameGeometry().topLeft(), contentToFrameSize(client)));
+    markStale(); // PowOS: every buffer, at the new scale (no longer redrawn by a later offer by itself)
     scheduleRender(); // drawn at the task's scale until the client commits its new size
 }
 
@@ -934,7 +937,11 @@ QSize AnlandWindowTask::fullScreenTaskSize() const
     // before KWin's full screen took effect (an xdg toplevel is full screen only once it acks), so it equalled the
     // "floating" one and Dolphin was laid out at the cover's size, pillarboxed on the 2268x2440 screen (10-30 22:19).
     if (m_fullScreenAsked) {
-        return task;
+        // PowOS: until the app's full-screen size comes (it sends it on KWin's "fullscreen 1"), the window keeps its
+        // own: the task was still the floating one, and the window went 504x606 logical for a moment - Broforce
+        // (a borderless window covering Wine's monitor) took that as leaving full screen, KWin said "fullscreen 0",
+        // and every tap of the button bounced straight back into the window (2026-11-02 21:35, five tries).
+        return (m_floatingTaskSize.isEmpty() || task != m_floatingTaskSize) ? task : QSize();
     }
     if (!m_appFullScreen || m_floatingTaskSize.isEmpty() || task != m_floatingTaskSize || !m_window) {
         return task;
@@ -978,14 +985,27 @@ void AnlandWindowTask::onBufferReady()
     eventfd_read(get_buffer_ready_fd(m_display), &val);
     m_offered = true;
     const int idx = get_selected_idx(m_display);
-    if (idx >= 0 && idx < m_bufCount && m_stale[idx]) {
+    // PowOS: only while the window's newest content isn't queued yet. A buffer is stale when it doesn't hold the newest
+    // content, but once ANOTHER buffer carried that content to the consumer, drawing this one too shows the same frame
+    // again: one game commit was drawn into every buffer in turn (Broforce 2026-11-02: 110 commits, 300 drawn per 5 s
+    // = a full-screen GPU composition 2.7x per game frame, on the GPU the game renders with, and later redraws sampled
+    // Xwayland's window buffer while it was being written for the next frame - KGSL has no implicit sync).
+    if (idx >= 0 && idx < m_bufCount && m_stale[idx] && !m_newestQueued) {
         scheduleRender();
     } else {
-        // Nothing new for it: hold it until the window changes (no frames while idle), answering in time.
+        // Nothing new for it: hold it until the window changes (no frames while idle), answering in time. The
+        // keepalive's render draws it first when it is stale, so the consumer never shows an older frame.
         m_keepalive.start();
     }
 }
 
+void AnlandWindowTask::markStale()
+{
+    // The window changed: no buffer holds its newest content, the next one offered is drawn (onBufferReady).
+    std::fill(std::begin(m_stale), std::end(m_stale), true);
+    m_newestQueued = false;
+}
+
 void AnlandWindowTask::scheduleRender()
 {
     if (!m_offered || m_renderScheduled) {
@@ -1025,6 +1045,7 @@ void AnlandWindowTask::render(bool keepalive)
         EGLNativeFence fence{egl->openglContext()->displayObject()};
         set_render_fence(m_display, fence.takeFileDescriptor().take());
         m_stale[idx] = false;
+        m_newestQueued = true;
         m_statFrames++;
         if (m_damagePending) {
             m_damagePending = false;
@@ -1520,10 +1541,21 @@ void AnlandWindowTasks::integrate()
         if (!task || !m_desktop || VirtualDesktopManager::self()->currentDesktop(window->output()) != m_desktop) {
             return; // the task's own focus (requestFocus, no desktop switch), or not exported
         }
-        send({QStringLiteral("open"), QString::number(task->id()), window->desktopFileName(), window->caption()});
+        send({QStringLiteral("open"), QString::number(task->id()), offeredAppId(window), window->caption()});
     });
 }
 
+QString AnlandWindowTasks::offeredAppId(const Window *window)
+{
+    // PowOS: who the window is to the app ("open"): its desktop file, else its X11 WM_CLASS class (KWin's
+    // resourceClass, lower case). Steam's and a Proton game's X windows name no desktop file: they were offered as ""
+    // and the app's launch placeholder for "steam" never got its window - Steam showed as two windows, the spinner
+    // and Steam (2026-11-02 21:33). The app matches a class like a desktop id (StartupWMClass, LinuxApp.matches) and
+    // a game's steam_app_<id> to the entry that starts it (RunningApps.isOf).
+    const QString file = window->desktopFileName();
+    return file.isEmpty() ? window->resourceClass() : file;
+}
+
 bool AnlandWindowTasks::handBackAndroidApp(Window *window)
 {
     // An Android app shown as a PowOS window (powos-android-app: scrcpy, app id android-<package>): full screen is the
@@ -1795,7 +1827,7 @@ bool AnlandWindowTasks::show(Window *window, bool fullScreen)
         task->focus();
         // Already a task: to the front - as what it is: a game's own full-screen task stays full screen (the drawer's
         // launch of a game that KWin already showed full screen made it a floating task, the game scaled into it).
-        QStringList open{QStringLiteral("open"), QString::number(task->id()), window->desktopFileName(), window->caption()};
+        QStringList open{QStringLiteral("open"), QString::number(task->id()), offeredAppId(window), window->caption()};
         if (task->fullScreen()) {
             open.append(QStringLiteral("fullscreen"));
         }
@@ -1817,7 +1849,7 @@ bool AnlandWindowTasks::show(Window *window, bool fullScreen)
                             << "of" << (parent->window() ? parent->window()->caption() : QString()) << ")";
         send({QStringLiteral("parent"), QString::number(id), QString::number(parent->id())});
     }
-    QStringList open{QStringLiteral("open"), QString::number(id), window->desktopFileName(), window->caption()};
+    QStringList open{QStringLiteral("open"), QString::number(id), offeredAppId(window), window->caption()};
     if (fullScreen) {
         open.append(QStringLiteral("fullscreen"));
     }
diff --git a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.h b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.h
index 3fda6e7..088ebc5 100644
--- a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.h
+++ b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.h
@@ -146,6 +146,7 @@ private:
     void onBufferReady();
     void onInputReadable();
     void processInputEvent(const InputEvent &ev);
+    void markStale();
     void scheduleRender();
     void render(bool keepalive);
     void watchWindow(Window *window);
@@ -207,6 +208,7 @@ private:
     std::shared_ptr<GLTexture> m_textures[MAX_BUFS];
     std::unique_ptr<GLFramebuffer> m_fbos[MAX_BUFS];
     bool m_stale[MAX_BUFS] = {};
+    bool m_newestQueued = false; // PowOS: a buffer with the window's newest content went to the consumer (markStale)
     QSize m_bufferSize;
     QSize m_taskSize; // resizeTo's, empty until the app says one
     QSize m_floatingTaskSize; // the task's size when its window went full screen (setAppFullScreen), until it changes
@@ -300,6 +302,7 @@ private:
      */
     AnlandWindowTask *relatedTask(const Window *window) const;
     /** An Android app's own window (powos-android-app): back to Android, the app itself in front. */
+    static QString offeredAppId(const Window *window);
     bool handBackAndroidApp(Window *window);
     void watchFullScreen(Window *window);
     void onFullScreenChanged(Window *window);
